############ 4. section 5.3: uniform expansion (5.9) and constants (5.10)
Im log(1 + d e^{-it})            = d*(d*cos(t) - 1)*sin(t)
|d + e^{it}|                     = -d**2*cos(t)**2/2 + d**2/2 + d*exp(I*t)/2 + d*exp(-I*t)/2 + 1
delta = arccos(|d+e^{it}|/2)     = sqrt(3)*d**2*exp(2*I*t)/36 - sqrt(3)*d**2/9 + sqrt(3)*d**2*exp(-2*I*t)/36 - sqrt(3)*d*exp(I*t)/6 - sqrt(3)*d*exp(-I*t)/6 + pi/3

a_+(t) = d-coeff of alpha_+(t)-(t+kappa) = -sqrt(3)*exp(I*t)/6 - sin(t) - sqrt(3)*exp(-I*t)/6
a_-(t) = d-coeff of alpha_-(t)-(t-kappa) = sqrt(3)*exp(I*t)/6 - sin(t) + sqrt(3)*exp(-I*t)/6
  matches paper (5.9) line 1:  a_+ = -sin t - cos t/sqrt3 : True    a_- = -sin t + cos t/sqrt3 : True

d-coefficient of F, a_+(t+kappa) - a_-(t+kappa) = -2*sqrt(3)*cos(t + pi/3)/3
  equals (2/sqrt3) sin(t - pi/6)     : True
  equals -(2/sqrt3) cos(t + kappa)   : True
  NOTE: a_+(t) - a_-(t+kappa) = -sqrt(3)*exp(I*t)/6 - sqrt(3)*exp(-I*t - I*pi/3)/6 - sqrt(3)*exp(I*t + I*pi/3)/6 + cos(t + pi/6) - sqrt(3)*exp(-I*t)/6  vanishes identically -- so the O(d) term genuinely uses a_+(t+kappa), as printed.

=== full nonlinear check: |F(t) - t - d*c1(t)| = O(d^2) ===
sup over grid of |F(t)-t-d c1(t)|/d^2  = 0.722656039844
  => O(d^2) remainder of (5.9) is uniform; (5.10) holds with c_0 = 1 - O(d).

=== (5.10): max over six phases spaced by kappa ===
min over t of max_j sin(t - j pi/3 - pi/6) = 0.866025403784439
min over t of max_j cos(t - j pi/3 - pi/6) = 0.866025403784439
sqrt(3)/2 = 0.866025403784439
  both equal sqrt(3)/2 exactly, so c_0 = (2/sqrt3)(sqrt3/2) = 1 - O(d).

